 "lines": [
  "The car hit the water.",
  "December. Black ice. Kai's car slid into a lake.",
  "@am_echo: \"The door won't open!\"",
  "Water presses on it with hundreds of pounds of force.",
  "@am_echo: \"Call nine one one!\"",
  "@af_heart: \"No phones! We have about one [minute](minnit)!\"",
  "A car usually floats for only about a [minute](minnit).",
  "Rescue experts teach three words. Seatbelts. Windows. Out.",
  "@af_heart: \"Seatbelts off! Now!\"",
  "Then open a window, fast. Power windows usually work for thirty to sixty seconds.",
  "@am_michael: \"Mine's dead!\"",
  "So break the glass. A side window, near a corner.",
  "Never the windshield. It's laminated, and almost impossible to break.",
  "@af_heart: \"Kai! The window hammer!\"",
  "Crack. Side windows are usually tempered glass. They shatter.",
  "The heavy engine pulls the nose down first, so the last air is in the back.",
  "Out. Through the window, onto the roof, then swim for shore.",
  "@am_echo: \"Why didn't we just wait for help?\"",
  "@af_heart: \"Help can't get there in one [minute](minnit).\"",
  "About four hundred people die in sinking cars in North America every year.",
  "For decades, people were told to wait for the car to fill, so the door would open.",
  "Experts now say that was wrong. By then, there's almost no air left.",
  "Kids in the car? Unbuckle them and push them out first, oldest to youngest.",
  "@am_michael: \"Never wait. Not once the car hit the water.\""
 ],
